 not None:\n        details.append(f\"pid={pid}\")\n    if started_at:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"The narrowest viable design is becoming clear: add a runtime-backed `subagent_states` collection, make subagent lifecycle updates target a specific worker id instead of a singleton slot, and teach only the `implementing` executor to fan out deterministically from the task plan. I’m validating the existing interruption/status plumbing next so recovery and fast-status don’t regress when more than one worker is active."}}
