{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_93","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'litehive report --verdict pass --role swe --step implementing --task-id T-0106 --message $'\"'Implemented parallel SWE fanout for the implementing stage from deterministic task plan items, added persisted per-worker runtime state (\"'`subagent_states`) plus worker identity/assignment metadata, and updated status/web observability to surface multiple active/recent workers instead of collapsing to a single active/last slot. The implementing executor now launches one worker per non-empty plan item when there is more than one item, waits for all launched workers to reach a terminal state before returning the stage verdict, aggregates worker reports into a single implementing report, and preserves recoverable stage-local worker context on interruption.'\"\\\\n\\\\nVerification run:\\\\n- \"'`uv run pytest -q tests/test_tasks_and_subagents.py` -> 33 passed'\"\\\\n- \"'`uv run pytest -q tests/test_runner_workflow.py` -> 94 passed'\"\\\\n- \"'`uv run pytest -q tests/test_observability_and_status.py -k \"render_task_summary_includes_active_subagent_pid or read_session_view_prefers_live_logs_for_active_subagent or build_workspace_snapshot_includes_active_subagent_artifacts or multiple_active_subagents\"` -> 3 passed'\"\\\\n- \"'`python -m compileall litehive tests/test_runner_workflow.py tests/test_tasks_and_subagents.py tests/test_observability_and_status.py` -> passed'\"\\\\n\\\\nEvidence against acceptance criteria:\\\\n- Successful fanout is covered by a new runner test that verifies implementing launches \"'`worker-01` and `worker-02`, waits for both before testing starts, and writes an aggregated implementing report.'\"\\\\n- Live persisted worker state is covered by a new subagent-manager test that runs two workers concurrently and verifies both running worker states, PIDs, worker keys, assignments, and session metadata are persisted before either worker finishes.\\\\n- Multi-worker observability is covered by a new status/snapshot test that verifies \"'`render_task_summary()` and `build_workspace_snapshot()` show two active workers for one task.'\"\\\\n- Interrupted fanout recoverability is covered by a new runner test that leaves the task at \"'`implementing` with persisted completed/interrupted worker context instead of ambiguous single-worker state.'\"\\\\n\\\\nSTAGE_RESULT:\\\\n{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Added implementing-stage parallel worker fanout with persisted per-worker runtime state and multi-worker observability.\\\",\\\"files_changed\\\":[\\\"litehive/cli.py\\\",\\\"litehive/main.py\\\",\\\"litehive/models.py\\\",\\\"litehive/observability.py\\\",\\\"litehive/runtime.py\\\",\\\"litehive/subagents.py\\\",\\\"litehive/tasks.py\\\",\\\"litehive/web.py\\\",\\\"tests/test_observability_and_status.py\\\",\\\"tests/test_runner_workflow.py\\\",\\\"tests/test_tasks_and_subagents.py\\\"],\\\"tests\\\":{\\\"added\\\":4,\\\"passing\\\":130},\\\"warnings\\\":[\\\"A full \"'`tests/test_observability_and_status.py` run was started but did not produce a completion result within the polling window; targeted observability slices covering the changed multi-worker paths passed.\"],\"follow_up_tasks\":[],\"acceptance_criteria\":[\"The implementing stage can launch more than one SWE worker for a single task from a deterministic local plan and waits for all launched workers before advancing.\",\"Litehive persists per-worker runtime state and artifacts during fanout, including worker identity, role/engine, status, path, and recent progress.\",\"Status and web observability now surface multiple active or recent workers for the same task.\",\"Interrupted fanout remains recoverable at the same stage with persisted worker context.\",\"Focused tests cover successful fanout, live worker state persistence, multi-worker observability, and interrupted fanout behavior.\"]}'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
